# Normalise line endings so the repository is reproducible on any machine.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS:
#
# Git on Windows commonly runs with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to
# CRLF in the working copy on checkout. For most files that is harmless. For
# apps/api/docker-entrypoint.sh it is fatal: a CRLF shebang makes the kernel
# look for an interpreter literally named "/bin/sh\r", and the container dies
# with "bad interpreter: no such file or directory".
#
# Without this file the project builds on the machine that wrote it and breaks
# for anyone who clones it on Windows - the exact failure risks R-05 and R-15
# are about.

# Store everything with LF in the repository; let Git decide the working copy.
* text=auto

# These must be LF in the WORKING COPY too, not just in the repository,
# because they are consumed by Linux tooling inside containers.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile    text eol=lf
docker-compose.yml text eol=lf
*.prisma        text eol=lf
.env.example    text eol=lf

# Generated, reviewed rarely - keep diffs collapsed in review tools.
package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated=true
